   "text": "```yaml\n- id: DR-01\n  requirement: >\n    The service must keep a record of every drone in the fleet and show whether each drone is in service, out of service for repair, or retired.\n- id: DR-02\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician add a drone to the fleet.\n- id: DR-03\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician retire a drone from the fleet.\n- id: DR-04\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician take a drone out of service for repair and later return it to service, recording both changes.\n- id: DR-05\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record each repair and servicing action on a drone, including what was done, who did it, and when.\n- id: DR-06\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician set up a charging pad at a site and record where that pad is.\n- id: DR-07\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician send a drone to charge and record when it was sent and when it finished.\n- id: DR-08\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not allow a drone that is out of service for repair to be assigned to a flight.\n- id: DR-09\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let the licensed dispatcher plan a flight by choosing which drone flies and the route it takes.\n- id: DR-10\n  requirement: >\n    The service must require the licensed person responsible for a flight to sign it off before it leaves, and must record who signed it off and when.\n- id: DR-11\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let the licensed person responsible for a flight call off a planned flight and must record the cancellation and the reason given.\n- id: DR-12\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a planned flight be handed from one person to another and must record who it was handed to.\n- id: DR-13\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not allow a flight to depart without a recorded sign-off from the licensed person responsible for it.\n- id: DR-14\n  requirement: >\n    The service must be able to produce, for any drone, a report of its full maintenance and repair history so the company can show a regulator how the drone has been looked after.\n- id: DR-15\n  requirement: >\n    Before the build is finalised, the team must interview the airspace desk and confirm the dispatcher's sign-off needs, because the interviews gave no usable detail on either, and no requirements for the airspace desk should be treated as confirmed until then.\n```"
